The event wait in every process. NullMoth's own change (not an upstream Mesa commit).
Waits on GPU work (vkWaitForFences and the channel's own waits) poll for their first millisecond exactly as before,
then sleep in the NVRM kext on the device's graphics completion event instead of polling; WindowServer keeps the
eager sleep it had. The rules are in nvkmd/nvrm/nvrm_evwait.h, a byte-for-byte copy of kexts/NVRM/nvrm_evwait.h
(tools/test_shared_headers.py compares them; tools/test_evwait_policy.c and tools/test_evwait_loop.c test them).
NVRM_EVENT_WAIT=0 in /Library/GPUBundles/nvmtl/nvrm610.conf turns the sleep off (polling as before).

